  "root_cause": {
    "concluded_at": "2026-10-13T15:20:00+08:00",
    "symptom": "OPEN_EVENT_CALENDAR_DETAIL failed 46 times (23 in the last 2 days); every failure is EVENT_CALENDAR_DETAIL_NOT_PROVEN with an identity mismatch.",
    "probe_result": "This probe reproduced the whole production path and ALL FOUR verifier conditions PASSED (first_failing_condition=None): readers and verifier are not broken.",
    "why_the_probe_passed_but_production_fails": "Today's first grid entry (除雪小分队, 1C9F9BD8F5) is OPEN, so its detail page prints a preview window (2026-10-13 00:00 - 2026-10-15 24:00) and the calendar title was read in full, so the exact-event-id path matched. Production picks the first STORE-uninspected entry, which is usually a NOT-YET-OPEN event - exactly the case whose attribution cannot succeed.",
    "chain": [
      "1. The resolver taps event_schedule.calendar_next_entry() = the first entry the STORE says is uninspected. Uninspected entries are mostly future events (open ones get inspected and stop being the next one).",
      "2. For a not-yet-open event the detail page prints no preview window, so match_calendar_detail_to_entry() bails at the start/end None check -> returns None -> attributed_event_id stays empty (observed empty in all sampled failures).",
      "3. The exact-id path cannot rescue it because _event_id() is sha1(OCR title)[:10] for unregistered events, and the calendar-side title is frequently a PARTIAL read: the failing frame shows the same real event as 除雪 (DC53E03FB8) on the calendar and 除雪小分队 (1C9F9BD8F5) on the detail -> two different ids for one event.",
      "4. next_detail_event_id is never written anywhere in the codebase (only read by the verifier), so the verifier's expectation always falls back to the first entry with tap_norm and details_observed not True, taken from the before-frame calendar."
    ],
    "secondary_defect_seen_in_the_same_frame": "The 2026-10-10 grid listed DISCOVERED_EVENT_6F33C054CA (英雄集结) TWICE with different date ranges (10/08..10/11 and 10/12..10/14) - one event_id for two occurrences. occurrence_key exists for this, but any consumer keyed on event_id alone will conflate them.",
    "fix_direction": "Do not gate attribution on the presence of a preview window: an unambiguous unique name match should be attributable on its own, and the not-yet-open case is precisely the one that needs it. Keep the date-overlap check as a tie-breaker/confirmation, not as a precondition. Separately, identity must not rest on a partial OCR string - either read the full bar text on the calendar side or reconcile by prefix/subset before hashing.",
    "evidence": [
      "evidence/event_calendar_detail_probe_20261013T145934Z.json (this probe: all four conditions PASS)",
      "episode 20261010_093019_922115 (expected DC53E03FB8 / actual 1C9F9BD8F5, attributed empty)",
      "offline re-read of that episode's before/after frames (entries + tap_norm)",
      "winter_agent_v2/event_calendar.py: _event_id (sha1 of the label), match_calendar_detail_to_entry (date-overlap precondition), runtime.py:5121 EVENT_CALENDAR_NEXT_DETAIL resolver",
      "learning/timed_event_schedule.json: DISCOVERED_EVENT_DC53E03FB8 carries current_blocker EVENT_NOT_OPEN (observed 2026-10-12T12:19:46Z)"
    ]
  }
